---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/profile-placeholder.svg';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Luis Amrein — Product Manager in Berlin"
  description="Luis Amrein is a Product Manager in Berlin with an engineering background. Prototypes, production code, digital health at Caspar Health, and the path into product."
  ogType="profile"
>
  <header class="page-hero shell">
    <p class="kicker">About Luis</p>
    <h1 class="display-title">Engineer by training.<br /><em>Product person by choice.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I am interested in the space where technical systems meet human behaviour—and in making that
      space a little easier to navigate.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section shell" aria-labelledby="story">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="portrait-placeholder">
        <Image
          src={portrait}
          alt="Editorial portrait placeholder for Luis; a current photograph will replace it"
          widths={[480, 720]}
          sizes="(max-width: 820px) 100vw, 40vw"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="about-copy">
        <p id="story">
          Product management is where my favourite things meet: empathy, design, technology,
          creativity, and evidence.
        </p>
        <p>
          I started in engineering, fascinated by how design and technology improve real-world
          systems. My bachelor’s thesis explored a head-up display for highly automated vehicles.
          During my master’s, I added ergonomics, medical technology, and management, then designed
          a knee-joint prosthesis for humanitarian use.
        </p>
        <p>
          Operations management gave me a practical education in agile work, data analysis, and
          process design. Working closely with product managers showed me a role that connected the
          technical and human sides of a problem. I made the switch and have not looked back.
        </p>
        <p>
          Since then, I have worked across healthcare staffing, sustainability products, internal
          operations platforms, marketplaces, and digital health. I am most useful when a problem
          is complex, several perspectives need to align, and the team needs a clear next move.
        </p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button" href="mailto:luis.amrein@hotmail.de">Say hello</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/luis-amrein/">
            View LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell" id="outside-work" aria-labelledby="outside-heading">
    <div class="section-heading reveal">
      <p class="section-label">Outside work</p>
      <h2 id="outside-heading">A very Berlin mix of motion, music, and <em>making.</em></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="interest-grid reveal">
      <article class="interest">
        <span class="interest-index">01</span>
        <h3>Gravel rides</h3>
        <p>Summer routes to the many lakes around Brandenburg—ideally with a good swim at the end.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="interest">
        <span class="interest-index">02</span>
        <h3>Every sport</h3>
        <p>Yoga, HIIT, volleyball, squash, table tennis. Urban Sports probably loses money on me.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="interest">
        <span class="interest-index">03</span>
        <h3>Music</h3>
        <p>Learning piano from my mum and, because this is Berlin, mixing music whenever I can.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="interest">
        <span class="interest-index">04</span>
        <h3>Portuguese</h3>
        <p>Still learning. Always open to a language tandem and patient corrections.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="interest">
        <span class="interest-index">05</span>
        <h3>Making things</h3>
        <p>DIY projects for my flat—another place where a rough prototype beats a long discussion.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="interest">
        <span class="interest-index">06</span>
        <h3>Curiosity</h3>
        <p>Long podcasts, new tools, unfamiliar systems, and the inevitable side project.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="personal-band">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">The short version</p>
      <h2>Serious about work.<br /><span class="scribble">Not myself.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      Yes, this can sound suspiciously like the next-door consultant checklist. I also spend time
      doing absolutely nothing—this page is simply trying to make a good impression.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
